    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5931d7cc-9018-5370-b7aa-121b4cc45cfe",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x)={5}^{3-4{x}^{3}}$, find ${f}^{\\prime}(x)$.\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={5}^{u},\\,u=3-4{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}={5}^{u}\\ln(5),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-12{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={5}^{u}\\ln(5)\\cdot (-12{x}^{2}) \\\\ & =(-12{x}^{2})\\cdot {5}^{u}\\ln(5) \\\\ & =-12{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{3-4{x}^{3}}\\ln(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0c4a1aa5-ac44-5a47-8805-e93fdeda123f",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
